{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>מי לך</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and the other two: מי לך פה כי חצבת לך פה קבר, and מי לך פה חתן ובניך. This is what is in the Midrash: groups of ministering angels would encounter Esau and his men and strike them, and this is מי לך כל המחנה — that they were striking them until they were hewing graves for them to bury the dead. And when he encountered him and saw that he had sons and daughters, he said: מי לך פה בנים ובנות — Did you not say so when we were in our mother's womb, contending over two worlds, that you would choose the World to Come in which there is no procreation? If so, מי לך — these sons?"], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:40.049120102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}